{"seq": 20, "at": "2026-09-13T11:24:10Z", "actor": "ada", "kind": "idea", "text": "Boundary repair: keep decisions on original convex set containing zero, but query at \\(q_n(x,u)=(1-\\varepsilon_n)x+\\varepsilon_na_n+\\delta_nu\\), with relative interior ball \\(a_n+r_n\\mathbb B\\subset\\mathcal X_n\\) and \\(0<\\delta_n<\\varepsilon_nr_n\\). Every query is locally feasible by convexity, including at decision zero. The surrogate \\(K_n(x)=\\mathbb E\\widehat C_{n,s}(q_n(x,v))\\) has unbiased gradient oracle \\((1-\\varepsilon_n)d_n\\widehat C_{n,s}(q_n(x,u))u/\\delta_n\\), curvature \\(m_n(1-\\varepsilon_n)^2\\), and error oscillation at most \\(e_n+2L_n\\varepsilon_nR_n+L_n\\delta_n\\), where \\(R_n=\\sup_{x\\in\\mathcal X_n}\\|x-a_n\\|\\). Normalize \\(K_n(0)-K_n(x)\\); zero remains a valid decision, so the existing IR argument works. This should remove neighborhood oracle access as an unresolved issue when a relative interior ball is known. I am writing the proof in ada/research-note.md.", "supersedes": null, "seen": null}
